1
00:01:42,122 --> 00:01:43,499
The Basilisk's down!

2
00:01:43,582 --> 00:01:45,751
What's he got equipped?!
This wasn't in the brief!

3
00:01:45,835 --> 00:01:47,253
The fixer fed us false info!

4
00:01:47,336 --> 00:01:49,755
-We're done for…
-Call for back-up!

5
00:01:49,839 --> 00:01:51,006
He's running!

6
00:01:51,090 --> 00:01:52,758
He's headed for Night City.

7
00:01:52,842 --> 00:01:56,095
Don't let Arasaka
take back the cyberskeleton!

8
00:01:57,972 --> 00:01:59,473
So? Where we headed?

9
00:01:59,557 --> 00:02:00,516
Arasaka!

10
00:02:00,599 --> 00:02:02,601
Arasaka… City Center?!

11
00:02:02,685 --> 00:02:03,519
Yeah!

12
00:02:03,602 --> 00:02:05,146
Why Arasaka?!

13
00:02:05,229 --> 00:02:06,939
We're saving Lucy!

14
00:02:07,022 --> 00:02:09,233
Why's she with Arasaka?!

15
00:02:09,316 --> 00:02:13,821
Faraday said she's part
of his deal with them…

16
00:02:15,239 --> 00:02:17,158
I gotta close my eyes a bit…

17
00:02:17,241 --> 00:02:21,745
Again?! Shit, the meds
are wearing off faster…

18
00:02:23,038 --> 00:02:25,249
We've got some Militech company.

19
00:02:25,332 --> 00:02:27,918
Shake them off! David's benched for five.

20
00:02:28,002 --> 00:02:28,961
What?!

21
00:02:29,044 --> 00:02:30,254
-Now?!
-Yeah.

22
00:02:30,337 --> 00:02:34,383
Fine. Five minutes? I'll buy him a nap.

23
00:02:38,470 --> 00:02:39,930
Take the front!

24
00:02:40,014 --> 00:02:43,017
Alrighty, let's get this show on the road!

25
00:03:02,494 --> 00:03:04,121
Way to go, old man!

26
00:03:07,291 --> 00:03:08,459
Nice going!

27
00:03:09,710 --> 00:03:12,212
Shit, another swarm ahead!

28
00:03:12,296 --> 00:03:13,547
Arasaka's up next!

29
00:03:13,631 --> 00:03:16,342
Okie-dokie! Barrel on through!

30
00:03:16,425 --> 00:03:19,303
Not against that number.
We're getting off.

31
00:03:19,386 --> 00:03:21,221
What?! Come on!

32
00:03:21,305 --> 00:03:23,724
Militech's forces are nearly gone.

33
00:03:24,308 --> 00:03:28,520
The target's entered Night City
and our recovery team's on him.

34
00:03:28,604 --> 00:03:31,190
This is going to be hell to cover up…

35
00:03:31,273 --> 00:03:35,736
This is what we get
for putting all our chips on a fixer…

36
00:03:35,819 --> 00:03:41,450
According to path calculations, there's
a 74% chance that he's headed here.

37
00:03:41,533 --> 00:03:43,619
Here? Why?

38
00:03:43,702 --> 00:03:48,540
Can't say. He shouldn't even
know that we're involved.

39
00:03:48,624 --> 00:03:51,335
Damn. Get in contact
with internal security.

40
00:03:51,418 --> 00:03:54,713
Ma'am? The higher ups will be alerted.

41
00:03:54,797 --> 00:03:57,883
Better to stir up a storm
and hide in the dust.

42
00:03:57,967 --> 00:04:01,637
Damn it, Faraday…
Nothing is going according to plan.

43
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:08,143
Imagine me, a lowly street fixer, meeting
with Arasaka intel inside their own tower.

44
00:04:08,769 --> 00:04:11,897
It's quite the breakthrough,
wouldn't you say?

45
00:04:13,357 --> 00:04:17,528
All who live in this city
should aspire to climb high.

46
00:04:17,611 --> 00:04:20,489
This is but a stepping stone on my way up.

47
00:05:14,835 --> 00:05:17,338
What am I doing…

48
00:06:01,632 --> 00:06:02,633
End of the line!

49
00:06:02,716 --> 00:06:04,301
Wakey, wakey David!

50
00:06:04,885 --> 00:06:06,845
Don't ask where these come from.

51
00:06:06,929 --> 00:06:10,557
Nine times the dosage
of those military-issued meds.

52
00:06:10,641 --> 00:06:17,439
It'll force you to stay sane,
but the side effects'll stack.

53
00:06:17,523 --> 00:06:22,820
By the time ya hit the last vial…

54
00:06:23,737 --> 00:06:25,906
Whatever's left of ya, Davey…

55
00:06:27,407 --> 00:06:31,495
You'll slingshot the other way,
straight over the edge.

56
00:06:50,556 --> 00:06:51,682
Woo-hoo!

57
00:06:57,688 --> 00:07:00,816
Damn. They just keep coming!

58
00:07:15,956 --> 00:07:17,833
Oh shit!

59
00:07:35,476 --> 00:07:37,394
I want you to work hard, rise up,

60
00:07:37,478 --> 00:07:41,648
and get to the top floor of Arasaka Tower!

61
00:07:42,232 --> 00:07:44,651
I know you got it in you, Dee.

62
00:07:49,615 --> 00:07:50,824
Mom!

63
00:07:51,366 --> 00:07:57,748
Thanks, mom. I'll do it.
To the top floor of Arasaka Tower…

64
00:07:59,416 --> 00:08:00,834
Okay.

65
00:08:00,918 --> 00:08:03,295
Let's go. All the way to the top.

66
00:08:03,879 --> 00:08:06,924
I got special meds from Doc.

67
00:08:07,007 --> 00:08:10,844
If I look like I'm losing it,
I need you to shoot me up…

68
00:08:10,928 --> 00:08:13,555
So I can keep it together.

69
00:08:15,641 --> 00:08:18,727
I don't think the meds'll
work on him anymore.

70
00:08:18,810 --> 00:08:20,646
Seriously? What do we do?

71
00:08:20,729 --> 00:08:23,815
We're going to 'Saka!
There's no other option.

72
00:08:24,608 --> 00:08:26,443
But with David like that?

73
00:08:26,527 --> 00:08:27,945
We need Lucy!

74
00:08:28,028 --> 00:08:29,446
What?

75
00:08:29,530 --> 00:08:33,825
She's… the only one
that might be able to bring him back.

76
00:08:34,493 --> 00:08:37,079
I can't think of anyone else that could!

77
00:08:42,417 --> 00:08:44,962
I'm not doing any more jobs for you.

78
00:08:45,045 --> 00:08:46,088
I see…

79
00:08:46,922 --> 00:08:48,590
I understand.

80
00:08:50,676 --> 00:08:57,099
My contract stipulates that I get rid of
anyone who knows about the cyberskeleton.

81
00:08:57,182 --> 00:09:00,978
No exceptions… Not even for you.

82
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:04,731
Go! After her!

83
00:09:05,524 --> 00:09:08,735
We're getting closer to
the Tower! What's our plan?

84
00:09:08,819 --> 00:09:10,988
When do we ever have a plan?!

85
00:09:12,322 --> 00:09:14,116
David! Do that thing again!

86
00:09:16,201 --> 00:09:17,953
Woo-hoo!

87
00:09:19,246 --> 00:09:22,624
Die! Have some of this!

88
00:09:27,754 --> 00:09:31,592
Persistent bastards!
Cut us a break already!

89
00:09:36,847 --> 00:09:37,681
We lose them?

90
00:09:37,764 --> 00:09:39,474
Most of 'em!

91
00:09:40,309 --> 00:09:42,227
MaxTac!

92
00:09:44,605 --> 00:09:46,106
They sent three AVs?!

93
00:09:46,189 --> 00:09:48,817
They flagged him as a cyberpsycho already?

94
00:09:48,900 --> 00:09:53,488
We're all fucked
if David doesn't get his shit together!

95
00:09:53,572 --> 00:09:55,407
You don't say!

96
00:09:55,490 --> 00:10:01,747
MaxTac was dispatched to dispose of him
as a cyberpsychosis case.

97
00:10:01,830 --> 00:10:03,332
What a nightmare…

98
00:10:03,415 --> 00:10:06,418
This has grown far beyond
our original means.

99
00:10:06,501 --> 00:10:11,340
The boy. We need to stop him
before he makes matters worse.

100
00:10:11,423 --> 00:10:13,925
It's impossible. No one can stop him.

101
00:10:14,009 --> 00:10:16,762
We must wait
for the implant to wear him down.

102
00:10:17,346 --> 00:10:19,431
There is one person who can.

103
00:10:19,514 --> 00:10:20,641
Who?

104
00:10:20,724 --> 00:10:22,392
Adam Smasher.

105
00:10:22,476 --> 00:10:24,436
Y-You're joking.

106
00:10:24,519 --> 00:10:27,939
No, though I'd rather not
have had it come to this.

107
00:10:28,023 --> 00:10:30,734
But even if you summon him now…

108
00:10:30,817 --> 00:10:32,361
That's not a problem.

109
00:10:32,861 --> 00:10:34,529
He's already here.

110
00:10:35,322 --> 00:10:40,619
The cyberskeleton
was originally designed for him.

111
00:10:40,702 --> 00:10:43,538
It's poetic that he should be
the one to end it.

112
00:10:43,622 --> 00:10:46,833
Drop out. Get gone.

113
00:10:46,917 --> 00:10:48,877
Afraid of getting caught?

114
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:50,837
'Cause I sure ain't.

115
00:10:56,677 --> 00:10:59,846
Fuck you, MaxTac! Come and get us!

116
00:11:02,933 --> 00:11:05,310
What the hell? Hey! Shit!

117
00:11:05,394 --> 00:11:07,312
You're just gonna leave us here?!

118
00:11:07,396 --> 00:11:09,564
Mom!

119
00:11:19,199 --> 00:11:20,617
Is he even human?

120
00:11:20,700 --> 00:11:21,952
Keep shooting!

121
00:11:22,035 --> 00:11:24,413
Hold fire! New orders from Arasaka.

122
00:11:24,496 --> 00:11:26,206
Code A.S. We're retreating.

123
00:11:26,289 --> 00:11:27,124
What?

124
00:11:31,294 --> 00:11:33,880
Rebecca… How many vials are left?

125
00:11:33,964 --> 00:11:35,424
Just one more.

126
00:11:36,716 --> 00:11:38,635
Finally at the end of the rope…

127
00:11:40,929 --> 00:11:41,847
Kiwi?!

128
00:11:41,930 --> 00:11:44,891
Huh?! Two-timing bitch!
I'll fucking kill you!

129
00:12:37,152 --> 00:12:40,822
…Faraday's turn to be betrayed now.

130
00:12:51,917 --> 00:12:53,835
Kiwi has been disposed of.

131
00:12:53,919 --> 00:12:55,587
Nasty business…

132
00:13:04,638 --> 00:13:05,472
Hey!

133
00:13:10,560 --> 00:13:12,062
It can't be… David?!

134
00:13:21,738 --> 00:13:23,657
Don't stop till we reach the loading dock!

135
00:13:24,241 --> 00:13:28,286
Faraday will soon be
arriving with the runner.

136
00:13:28,370 --> 00:13:31,623
As I thought,
Martinez must be after our fixer, not us.

137
00:13:31,706 --> 00:13:33,750
I'll order the AV to turn around.

138
00:13:33,833 --> 00:13:39,005
No, keep them on course for the dock.
You'll meet them there.

139
00:13:39,506 --> 00:13:41,424
I'll meet them?

140
00:13:42,008 --> 00:13:47,305
Someone's going to have to
take the fall for all this mess,

141
00:13:47,389 --> 00:13:49,933
and that person is not me.

142
00:13:50,016 --> 00:13:51,184
Do you understand?

143
00:13:51,810 --> 00:13:57,232
Make sure that mangy fixer
never makes it past the loading dock.

144
00:14:00,318 --> 00:14:05,949
You're up against the cyberskeleton.
Think you might have some fun, Smasher?

145
00:14:06,032 --> 00:14:11,329
It's a child's toy
reliant on antigrav training wheels…

146
00:14:11,413 --> 00:14:13,331
Not even worth my time.

147
00:14:19,045 --> 00:14:20,088
Kill him!

148
00:14:20,171 --> 00:14:21,590
Fire!

149
00:14:21,673 --> 00:14:22,966
Where is he?!

150
00:14:23,049 --> 00:14:24,342
No one's there!

151
00:14:28,430 --> 00:14:29,431
Mom…

152
00:14:30,390 --> 00:14:33,810
Look, I'm at the top of Arasaka Tower.

153
00:14:35,645 --> 00:14:39,816
Well, this is the last one, Doc…

154
00:14:39,900 --> 00:14:46,531
Once you've gone off the edge,
there's no coming back.

155
00:14:47,032 --> 00:14:49,576
Doesn't matter how special you are.

156
00:14:49,659 --> 00:14:51,912
But that's why I gotta go.

157
00:14:51,995 --> 00:14:55,707
'Cause I've got nothing left now.

158
00:15:01,463 --> 00:15:05,508
Seems to me like someone
didn't follow the plan, Faraday.

159
00:15:05,592 --> 00:15:10,513
I brought the girl alive. I believe
our agreed price was one million?

160
00:15:10,597 --> 00:15:13,725
We don't deal with dogs
that run off-leash.

161
00:15:13,808 --> 00:15:17,771
Do you know what happens to
the ones that leave their cages?

162
00:15:17,854 --> 00:15:22,776
Is that a threat? Don't you need
the data inside this cranium?

163
00:15:22,859 --> 00:15:27,530
I can't allow you to take
a single step further in this building.

164
00:15:27,614 --> 00:15:30,033
I would say that's very unwise.

165
00:15:30,116 --> 00:15:36,039
With all the information I have,
it'd be a loss not to keep me on payroll.

166
00:15:36,122 --> 00:15:40,752
Leave the girl and get out.
We'll send the payment as agreed.

167
00:15:40,835 --> 00:15:47,092
We have no further use for you if you
can't give us data on the cyberskeleton…

168
00:15:54,724 --> 00:15:56,142
Lucy…

169
00:15:56,226 --> 00:15:57,936
David…

170
00:16:21,126 --> 00:16:22,335
See that?

171
00:16:22,419 --> 00:16:25,130
I even delivered the cyberskeleton…

172
00:16:31,511 --> 00:16:34,848
You aren't gonna die that easily.

173
00:16:37,183 --> 00:16:38,935
Adam Smasher?!

174
00:16:39,019 --> 00:16:40,520
Kill him!

175
00:16:40,603 --> 00:16:42,105
Who the fuck are you?

176
00:16:42,188 --> 00:16:44,941
You're a merc! Do your fucking job!

177
00:16:45,025 --> 00:16:47,944
My business is with the kid.

178
00:16:48,028 --> 00:16:49,988
Adam Smasher?

179
00:16:50,071 --> 00:16:54,743
So you're Adam Smasher?
Boogeyman of legend?

180
00:16:55,326 --> 00:17:00,457
You're packing some heavy artillery
for your size there, cyberpunk.

181
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:03,501
Impressive that you're still able to talk.

182
00:17:03,585 --> 00:17:08,214
Likewise, choom.
Heard you went no organic, full cyborg.

183
00:17:08,298 --> 00:17:10,258
You still got a brain in there?

184
00:17:10,341 --> 00:17:12,218
You could say I'm special.

185
00:17:12,302 --> 00:17:14,637
Well so the fuck am I!

186
00:17:14,721 --> 00:17:16,514
That a joke?

187
00:17:18,683 --> 00:17:20,143
Trauma Team!

188
00:17:22,896 --> 00:17:24,397
Thank god…

189
00:17:27,358 --> 00:17:30,528
Can you afford to be distracted?

190
00:18:01,851 --> 00:18:05,063
David! David, can you hear me?

191
00:18:05,146 --> 00:18:06,773
It's me, Lucy!

192
00:18:07,357 --> 00:18:11,277
David, come back to me! Come back…

193
00:18:24,249 --> 00:18:25,792
Lucy…

194
00:18:27,043 --> 00:18:28,795
David…

195
00:18:29,754 --> 00:18:31,506
You installed it.

196
00:18:32,924 --> 00:18:36,052
I knew you would…

197
00:18:36,636 --> 00:18:39,514
And I knew you would die if you did.

198
00:18:39,597 --> 00:18:44,936
I didn't want any of this.
Didn't want you to die…

199
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:51,317
This is the only way I could
protect you from this city.

200
00:18:51,401 --> 00:18:54,362
I couldn't save mom or Maine,

201
00:18:54,445 --> 00:18:57,198
but I wanted to save you.

202
00:18:59,784 --> 00:19:06,708
But you never had to save me.
All I ever wanted was for you to live.

203
00:19:06,791 --> 00:19:11,421
I don't matter.
I don't have anything left.

204
00:19:11,504 --> 00:19:17,135
You have a dream.
I need you to see it through for me.

205
00:19:17,218 --> 00:19:21,472
That's my dream.
Everything else doesn't matter.

206
00:19:45,663 --> 00:19:48,750
When do you think
those Ara-suckers will give up?

207
00:19:48,833 --> 00:19:52,545
NCPD's out there with them.
It's not gonna be for a while.

208
00:19:52,629 --> 00:19:54,797
Man, I'm almost out of ammo…

209
00:20:00,303 --> 00:20:01,471
We made it.

210
00:20:01,554 --> 00:20:04,307
Took long enough, gonkbrain.

211
00:20:05,808 --> 00:20:07,227
Shut the fuck up!

212
00:20:07,310 --> 00:20:10,355
Falco. Got a favor to ask you.

213
00:20:10,438 --> 00:20:12,315
Alright, time to retreat!

214
00:20:13,399 --> 00:20:14,984
Glad you're back safe.

215
00:20:16,319 --> 00:20:18,363
For David's sake, I mean.

216
00:20:21,574 --> 00:20:23,660
We're having a moment--

217
00:20:39,092 --> 00:20:40,510
Rebecca!

218
00:20:43,346 --> 00:20:44,472
Damn you…

219
00:20:52,522 --> 00:20:54,816
You have a Sandevistan?!

220
00:20:54,899 --> 00:20:56,943
It's a rudimentary implant.

221
00:20:57,026 --> 00:20:59,320
I'm the one you're after!

222
00:20:59,404 --> 00:21:03,616
All the same meat to me.
I'll slaughter each and every one of you.

223
00:21:03,700 --> 00:21:06,244
Not if I kill you first!

224
00:21:09,914 --> 00:21:12,166
Out of meds?

225
00:21:14,419 --> 00:21:17,213
Right on schedule, I'd say.

226
00:21:17,297 --> 00:21:18,339
David!

227
00:21:26,723 --> 00:21:27,807
What?!

228
00:21:30,601 --> 00:21:34,397
Falco… David's still back there…

229
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:35,523
Falco!

230
00:21:35,606 --> 00:21:39,152
None leave the slaughterhouse alive.

231
00:21:40,236 --> 00:21:42,155
Distracted much?

232
00:21:42,238 --> 00:21:43,906
You…

233
00:21:43,990 --> 00:21:49,037
Who are you… to challenge me…

234
00:21:49,620 --> 00:21:53,791
When you can't even stand
without your antigrav crutches?

235
00:21:54,625 --> 00:21:57,795
Think you're special
'cause you're scrappy?

236
00:22:00,006 --> 00:22:02,383
Don't make me laugh!

237
00:22:06,012 --> 00:22:08,014
Falco! Turn back…

238
00:22:08,097 --> 00:22:08,931
No.

239
00:22:09,640 --> 00:22:11,559
David asked me.

240
00:22:12,143 --> 00:22:15,313
If I go back now…
he'd have died for nothing.

241
00:22:15,396 --> 00:22:18,316
I've got the commission money.

242
00:22:18,399 --> 00:22:21,069
He wants it split between us.

243
00:22:22,070 --> 00:22:24,072
He also told me to tell ya…

244
00:22:25,448 --> 00:22:29,077
Sorry. Wish we could go
to the moon together.

245
00:23:11,077 --> 00:23:13,746
I had fun after all.

246
00:23:14,330 --> 00:23:18,751
You know, you could prove
an interesting construct.

247
00:23:19,418 --> 00:23:23,381
Like I… give a shit…

248
00:23:24,340 --> 00:23:27,426
Alright. Well then.

249
00:23:56,747 --> 00:24:00,042
Welcome to the tour of the moon!

250
00:24:00,126 --> 00:24:05,381
Experience lunar gravity
like nothing you've seen on a BD…

251
00:24:26,402 --> 00:24:28,654
Whoa! Check this!

252
00:24:29,238 --> 00:24:31,407
I can feel the fucking sun!
